# Q14 — clicking a declared attacker, and a box, pull attackers back.
#
# NOT `|Attacking` + `activephase=COMBAT_DECLARE_ATTACKERS`: that was this
# file's first design, and it is wrong for this claim. `GameState.applyGameOnThread`
# calls `handleCombat` for EITHER combat phase UNCONDITIONALLY (not only when
# a card is marked `|Attacking` — an empty attack is still a manual
# `GameEventAttackersDeclared`), which fires the "attackers declared" event
# itself and skips Forge's own live `InputAttack` entirely — the same shape
# of bug as the Declare Blockers one (`wave33-evidence/s3-blockers.md`), just
# with nobody attacking instead of a stale characteristic. The result: no
# `updateButtons` ever arrives for the live declare-attackers window, so a
# browser's "button2 === Call Back" precondition can never hold — there is
# no live window to hold it in.
#
# This file instead lands at seat 0's own Main Phase 1, with the creature on
# the battlefield UNTAPPED, NON-SICK, and plainly a creature — no `|Attacking`
# marker at all. The test presses priority forward through the ordinary main
# loop; Forge's own phase transition into Declare Attackers Step opens the
# REAL `InputAttack` for seat 0, live, with the creature offered. That is the
# window `Board.tsx`'s click-to-declare / click-to-undeclare / Call Back
# interaction actually needs — see `scenario-combat.jvm.test.ts` for exactly
# which clicks drive it.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Memnite
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
